WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcribed from the narration in this video. Every figure the
speaker states matches the OECD time-use data behind this page.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.980
Bonjour!

2
00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.760
You want to know how my day goes?

3
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:03.680
Sit down.

4
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.080
There's no rush here.

5
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.240
I wake up and I take my time.

6
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.200
Breakfast, a warm croissant,
butter, good coffee.

7
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.320
In France, we spend 12 hours and 32
minutes a day, just on personal care.

8
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.800
We believe the body
deserves attention.

9
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.260
Then I work, but not like crazy.

10
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.000
I do about 3 hours and 24
minutes of paid work a day.

11
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.020
We work around 1,487 hours a year.

12
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.720
Enough to live, not
enough to forget how to.

13
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.180
After that, there's
the invisible work.

14
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.100
Cooking a real meal, tidying up,
maybe helping a neighbour.

15
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.520
And then, leisure.

16
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.300
Almost 5 hours of it.

17
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.980
I read, I walk, I sit at a café and
watch people argue about cheese.

18
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.520
4 hours and 53 minutes,
every single day.

19
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.180
Oh, and the best part?

20
00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.560
Most of us retire by 61.

21
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.100
You see, in France,
the day is not a race.

22
00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.251
It's a meal, and we
take every course.
